FILE..LLMDD/spec-driven/bugs/bug-5-advisor-writes-without-approval.md=SIZE:6877,MIME:text/markdown,ENCODING:UTF-8,LANG:Markdown,EXT:md
CODEX..LLMDD/spec-driven/bugs/bug-5-advisor-writes-without-approval.md=HEADING:bug-5: Advisor writes without approval
CODEX..LLMDD/spec-driven/bugs/bug-5-advisor-writes-without-approval.md=HEADING:Bug detail
CODEX..LLMDD/spec-driven/bugs/bug-5-advisor-writes-without-approval.md=HEADING:EXPECTED: a deterministic gate — e.g. Advisor has no write-capable tools
CODEX..LLMDD/spec-driven/bugs/bug-5-advisor-writes-without-approval.md=HEADING:at all (no edit\, no bash/file-writes)\, or a permission-escalation hook
CODEX..LLMDD/spec-driven/bugs/bug-5-advisor-writes-without-approval.md=HEADING:that blocks on missing Designer approval token.
CODEX..LLMDD/spec-driven/bugs/bug-5-advisor-writes-without-approval.md=HEADING:ACTUAL: frontmatter grants `bash: allow` alongside `edit: deny`\, and the
CODEX..LLMDD/spec-driven/bugs/bug-5-advisor-writes-without-approval.md=HEADING:no-implementation rule lives only in prompt text (agent md + system
CODEX..LLMDD/spec-driven/bugs/bug-5-advisor-writes-without-approval.md=HEADING:tensor). Bash is a write-capable channel (`echo x > file`\, `apply_patch`\,
CODEX..LLMDD/spec-driven/bugs/bug-5-advisor-writes-without-approval.md=HEADING:`python3 -c "open(...\,'w')..."`)\, so the constraint is advisory\, not
CODEX..LLMDD/spec-driven/bugs/bug-5-advisor-writes-without-approval.md=HEADING:enforced. No approval-token check exists anywhere in the repo.
CODEX..LLMDD/spec-driven/bugs/bug-5-advisor-writes-without-approval.md=HEADING:EXPECTED: a machine-checkable approval requirement.
CODEX..LLMDD/spec-driven/bugs/bug-5-advisor-writes-without-approval.md=HEADING:ACTUAL: no hits — approval is an unwritten convention\, not a gate.
CODEX..LLMDD/spec-driven/bugs/bug-5-advisor-writes-without-approval.md=HEADING:Fix summary (Resolved only)
CODEX..LLMDD/spec-driven/bugs/bug-5-advisor-writes-without-approval.md=HEADING:Tests proving resolution (Resolved only)
FILE..LLMDD/spec-driven/bugs/bug-4-layer-layout-demands-violated.md=SIZE:3048,MIME:text/markdown,ENCODING:UTF-8,LANG:Markdown,EXT:md
CODEX..LLMDD/spec-driven/bugs/bug-4-layer-layout-demands-violated.md=HEADING:bug-4: Layer layout demands violated
CODEX..LLMDD/spec-driven/bugs/bug-4-layer-layout-demands-violated.md=HEADING:Bug detail
CODEX..LLMDD/spec-driven/bugs/bug-4-layer-layout-demands-violated.md=HEADING:EXPECTED per demands: application/{services\,ports\,useCases}\,
CODEX..LLMDD/spec-driven/bugs/bug-4-layer-layout-demands-violated.md=HEADING:infrastructure/{one folder per port + Env adapter}\, domain/{models\,valueObjects}\,
CODEX..LLMDD/spec-driven/bugs/bug-4-layer-layout-demands-violated.md=HEADING:control/{dependencyInjection\,entryPoint}\, camelCase folders (Scala)\, no files in any layer root.
CODEX..LLMDD/spec-driven/bugs/bug-4-layer-layout-demands-violated.md=HEADING:ACTUAL:
CODEX..LLMDD/spec-driven/bugs/bug-4-layer-layout-demands-violated.md=HEADING:1. application/{ports\,services\,use_cases} — snake_case\, expected camelCase useCases.
CODEX..LLMDD/spec-driven/bugs/bug-4-layer-layout-demands-violated.md=HEADING:2. infrastructure/{database\,environment\,filesystem\,parsers} — 4 folders for 3 ports
